nly</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;\n                    <a href=\"javascript:window.print()\">Print</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<a href=\"product_types.php?site=LCH\">Product List</a>&nbsp;|&nbsp;\n                    <a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=1&glossary=1\">Glossary On</a></div>\n                <div>Versions:\n                            <b>1</b> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=2&glossary=0\">2</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=3&glossary=0\">3</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=4&glossary=0\">4</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=5&glossary=0\">5</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=6&glossary=0\">6</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=7&glossary=0\">7</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=8&glossary=0\">8</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=9&glossary=0\">9</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=10&glossary=0\">10</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=11&glossary=0\">11</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=12&glossary=0\">12</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=13&glossary=0\">13</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=14&glossary=0\">14</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=15&glossary=0\">15</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=16&glossary=0\">16</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=17&glossary=0\">17</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=18&glossary=0\">18</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=19&glossary=0\">19</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=20&glossary=0\">20</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=21&glossary=0\">21</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=22&glossary=0\">22</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=23&glossary=0\">23</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=24&glossary=0\">24</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=25&glossary=0\">25</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=26&glossary=0\">26</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=27&glossary=0\">27</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=28&glossary=0\">28</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=29&glossary=0\">29</a> \n                            \n<a href=\"?site=LCH&issuedby=LCH&product=AFD&format=CI&version=30&glossary=0\">30</a> \n                    <hr size=\"1\" width=\"520\" noshade=\"noshade\" align=\"left\" />\n        </div>\n        <pre class=\"glossaryProduct\">\n711\nFXUS64 KLCH 031117\nAFDLCH\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Lake Charles LA\n617 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\n...New AVIATION...\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n- Dewpoints will begin to rise through the work week, while both\n  high and low temperatures are forecast to remain at or slightly\n  above average.\n\n-Isolated diurnally driven afternoon thunderstorms will be\n possible each day through the work week, with rain chances in the\n 15 to 30% range.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\n(Today through Sunday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nAs mentioned in the AFD a mere 24h ago, the relatively short lived\nnortherly flow would be just that... short lived. While not a marked\nincrease, dewpoints have begun to creep upward early this Monday\nmorning. Much of the forecast area saw dewpoints fall into the mid\n60s yesterday thanks to the drier air behind the frontal boundary\nthat moved through Sunday morning. The boundary now lingers\nquasistationary along the coastline, where it is forecast to\nremain through the beginning of the workweek before lifting\nnorthward as a warm front by midweek. Winds today will be light\nand variable, but southerly flow will once again become\nestablished, allowing dewpoints to climb back into the mid to\nupper 70s.\n\nAloft, the area will reside between an upper level ridge expanding\nfrom the Desert SW into the Southern Plains and an upper cutoff\nlow over the SECONUS. Although the cutoff low will be somewhat\nreabsorbed into the broader flow, a weakness aloft will still be\npresent. The ridge will allow for parts of SETX to see a slight\nincrease in afternoon temps, though nothing climatologically\nsignificant. Increasing low level moisture, the subtle weakness\naloft, and daytime heating will support isolated convection\nthrough much of the workweek, especially across the eastern half\nof the CWA.\n\nTemperatures will remain slightly above normal and fairly uniform\nfrom day to day. A few locations, particularly across SETX where\nthe influence of the upper ridge will be greatest, could approach\nHeat Advisory criteria during the workweek. However, widespread\nheat hazards appear unlikely at this time.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...\n(12Z TAFS)\nIssued at 615 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nDry airmass left from the frontal passage yesterday will keep\nconditions hot and dry today. Winds will primarily be light and\nvariable as the region is situated in a limbo between features, ie\nnothing to drive wind speeds. Coastal terminals could see\nsoutherly winds with a seabreeze this afternoon. A moisture plume\nshould accompany any seabreeze passage and so VFR ceilings will\nlikely return today as well.\n\n11\n\n&&\n\n.MARINE...\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nA light west to southwest flow will continue through the next\ncouple of days, becoming more southerly by late Tuesday and\nbeyond. A few isolated showers will be possible later in the\nperiod, but overall mostly dry conditions are expected through the\nwork week.\n\n&&\n\n.FIRE WEATHER...\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nMinimum afternoon RH values today and Monday are expected to range\nfrom 35 to 50 percent. Winds will turn back out of the south on\nMonday. Isolated afternoon thunderstorms will be possible through\nmuch of the workweek.\n\n&&\n\n.LCH WATCHES/WARNINGS/ADVISORIES...\nLA...None.\nTX...None.\nGM...None.\n&&\n\n$$\n\nPUBLIC/FIRE/MARINE...87\nAVIATION...11\n\n\n</pre>\n\n                </div>\n            <footer>\n                                <div class=\"footer-legal\">\n    <div id=\"footerLogo\" class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-2 col-md-2\">\n        <a href=\"//www.usa.gov\"><img src=\"/css/images/usa_gov.png\" alt=\"usa.gov\" width=\"110\" height=\"30\" /></a>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-4 col-md-4\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled footer-legal-content\">\n            <li><a href=\"//www.commerce.gov\">US Dept of Commerce</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.noaa.gov\">National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov\">National Weather Service</a></li>\n                        <li>1325 East West Highway<br /></li>\n                        <li>Silver Spring, MD 20910</li>\n            <li><br /><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/Contact\">Comments? Questions? Please Contact Us.</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 col-md-3\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/disclaimer\">Disclaimer</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.cio.noaa.gov/services_programs/info_quality.html\">Information Quality</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/help\">Help</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"//www.weather.gov/glossary\">Glossary</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"col-xs-12 col-sm-3 col-md-3\">\n        <ul class=\"list-unstyled\">\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/privacy\">Privacy Policy</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.noaa.gov/foia-freedom-of-information-act\">Freedom of Information Act (FOIA)</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/about\">About Us</a></li>\n            <li><a href=\"https://www.weather.gov/careers\">Career Opportunities</a></li>\n        </ul>\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n            </footer>\n        </main>\n    </body>\n</html>\n",
